  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GALVANISING EFFORTS TOWARD RECOVERY OF THE MALAYAN TIGER (PANTHERA TIGRIS JACKSONI) IN MALAYSIA&apos;S SOUTHERN FOREST COMPLEX (2021-2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONSERVE AND SUSTAIN THE POPULATION OF TIGERS IN AND AROUND THE ENDAU-ROMPIN LANDSCAPE. PROJECT OBJECTIVES AND ACTIVITIES INCLUDE THE FOLLOWING: (1) STRENGTHEN WILDLIFE PROTECTION EFFORTS THROUGH IMPROVED COORDINATION AMONG AGENCIES THROUGH A SMART (SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL) PATROL DATA MANAGEMENT SYSTEM AMONG THE JOHOR WILDLIFE CONSERVATION PROJECT, CAPACITY BUILDING AND ON THE JOB TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE TO IMPLEMENT AN ANTI-POACHING AND PATROLLING STRATEGY IN THE ENDAU-ROMPIN LANDSCAPE, AND MONITOR AND GENERATE INFORMATION ON THREATS TO ADDRESS INFORMATION GAPS (2) MONITOR TIGER POPULATION TRENDS IN THE ENDAU-ROMPIN LANDSCAPE THROUGH A CAMERA TRAP SURVEY AND ESTIMATE TIGER POPULATION DENSITY AND (3) DEVELOP MANAGEMENT PLAN GUIDELINES TO SECURE TIGER HABITATS AND MAINTAIN CONNECTIVITY AT PRIORITY CORRIDORS.</narrative>
  </description>
